.TH CHMAP_CREATE_CH 3 "2026-09-20" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chmap_create_ch \- create a hash map with a custom hashing procedure
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chashmap.h>

chmap chmap_create_ch(size_t initial_bucket_array_size,
                      ccol_data_type key_type, ccol_data_type val_type,
                      ccol_hashing_proc_t custom_hashing_proc, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a hash map that hashes its keys with the supplied procedure. It is
a thin inline wrapper over chmap_create_full(3) that passes NULL for the
memory management procedures, so the map uses the default allocator.

The map picks its implementation strategy from the key and value types, as
chmap_create_full(3) describes; supplying a hashing procedure does not
change that choice.
.fi
.SH "CUSTOM HASHING"
.nf
The procedure receives the key bytes and their length, and returns an
unsigned long. It must return the same value for two keys that the map
considers equal; for a char * key, equal means equal contents, not an
equal pointer.

The length is the size that the map stores for that key:
  - For a char * key: strlen + 1.
  - For a key of a fixed size (an integer, a float, a double, a pointer
    or a struct): the sizeof() of the type.
  - For a key that goes through the raw layer, for example
    chmap_insert_elem(3): cmap_pair.size.
The procedure therefore needs no terminator and no rule of its own to
find the end of a key, and it can hash a binary key whose length is
known only at run time.

The return value does not need to avalanche, because the map finalizes
the value that the procedure returns with its own bit-mixing step before
it reduces the value to a bucket or a slot. A procedure that puts all of
its entropy in the low bits (a sum, a small identifier, a truncated
checksum) therefore still distributes correctly, and the contract is
simply any function of the key that respects equality.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
initial_bucket_array_size  Initial capacity hint
key_type                   Key type, as a ccol_data_type
val_type                   Value type, as a ccol_data_type
custom_hashing_proc        Hashing procedure, or NULL to use the map's own
                           hashing for the key type
err                        Optional pointer that receives an error string on
                           failure, or NULL
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A newly created map on success.
NULL on failure, with *err set to an error string when err is non-NULL.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Failure is reported rather than fatal; the chmap_construct_ch(3) macro
layer calls ccol_fatal_err() instead
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chmap_create (3),
.BR chmap_create_full (3),
.BR chmap_construct_ch (3),
.BR chmap_init_ch (3),
.BR chmap_destroy (3)
